Table cell accessible: take the SolarMutex before the disposed check in getAccessibleName.

AccessibleCell::getAccessibleName called ensureAlive() before taking the SolarMutex, so a call from
an accessibility bridge running without the SolarMutex (gtk3) could pass the check, wait while
another thread disposed the cell (table rows changed, document closed), and then name a disposed
cell. Same lock-order bug as the sd slide sorter (hst-sd-slidesorter-a11y-lock-order.patch).
Upstream bug (same code in LibreOffice 26.8.1.1 and 26.8.3.1).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: CppunitTest_sd_a11y (hst-svx-table-cell-a11y-dispose-race-test.patch).
---
--- a/svx/source/table/accessiblecell.cxx
+++ b/svx/source/table/accessiblecell.cxx
@@ -411,8 +411,8 @@
 
 OUString SAL_CALL AccessibleCell::getAccessibleName()
 {
-    ensureAlive();
-    SolarMutexGuard aSolarGuard;
+    SolarMutexGuard aSolarGuard;
+    ensureAlive();
 
     if( pAccTable )
     {
